## 6. Clinical Safety Design

### 6.1 Human-in-the-Loop Requirement

No automated action is permitted at any risk tier. All outputs are decision-support tools. This is non-negotiable because:
1. NLP models have error rates — human judgment corrects them
2. Models cannot know about bereavement, family crisis, or physical illness
3. The counsellor reaching out IS the therapeutic intervention

### 6.2 False Negative Priority

In mental health screening, false negatives (missed at-risk individuals) are more harmful than false positives. The pipeline is tuned to accept higher false positive rates at Tier 1, using Tier 2 to reduce them before escalation.

### 6.3 Minimum Viable Safety Standards

Before any pilot deployment:
- [ ] IRB/ethics board approval
- [ ] Informed consent protocol (adolescents + parents/guardians)
- [ ] Counsellor training on pipeline outputs and cognitive bias
- [ ] Clear escalation pathways to school-based and emergency services
- [ ] Incident review process for missed crises
- [ ] Quarterly model revalidation against clinical outcomes
- [ ] Applicable data protection compliance review

